0,"_gp_insider_buying":false,"_score_insider_buying":0.0,"pf":[],"description_full":"Cummins Inc. offers various power solutions worldwide. The company operates through five segments: Engine, Distribution, Components, Power Systems, and Accelera. It offers diesel and natural gas-powered engines; and drivetrain systems, including axles, drivelines, brakes, and suspension systems; and on- and off-highway, and other products. The company also provides aftertreatment technology and solutions comprising custom engineering systems and integrated controls, oxidation catalysts, particulate filters, and selective catalytic reduction systems, as well as engineered components, including dosers; turbochargers, fuel systems, and valvetrain technologies; electronic control modules, sensors, and supporting software; and automated manual transmissions, and automatic transmissions for internal combustion engines. In addition, it sells and offers support services power generation systems, high-horsepower engines, and heavy-duty and medium-duty engines; offers application engineering services, custom-designed assemblies, and in-shop and field-based repair services; and retail and wholesale aftermarket parts. Further, the company offers standby and prime power generators, controls, paralleling systems, and transfer switches; turnkey solutions for distributed generation and energy management applications using natural gas, diesel, battery energy storage systems, and newer alternative sustainable fuels; diesel and natural gas high-speed, high-horsepower engines; and A/C generator/alternator products. Additionally, it provides electrified power systems, including batteries, fuel cells, and electric powertrain technologies. It sells its products to original equipment manufacturers, distributors, dealers, and other customers. The company was formerly known as Cummins Engine Company and changed its name to Cummins Inc. in 2001. Cummins Inc. was founded in 1919 and is headquartered in Columbus, Indiana.","ceo_bio":"Ms. Jennifer W. Rumsey | CEO & Chairman of the Board | Age 51 | Compensation: $8.6M (FY2025)","culture_narrative":"Employs approximately 67K people. Revenue per employee of $500K ranks in the above the sector median among Industrials peers, improving at 7%/yr \u2014 growing workforce leverage. Each employee generates $35K of free cash flow annually. Stock-based compensation of $1K per employee reflects an ownership culture. CEO compensation is 17\u00d7 revenue per employee (reasonable relative to workforce productivity). Governance score flags moderate compensation governance risk (4/10).","financial_summary":["Cummins Inc. is a large-cap industrials business with a $62.0B market cap on $33.7B of annual revenue.","The top line has compounded at +6% over the past three years and +6% annually across the full decade, a respectable pace for a business of this size.","Returns on capital run at 20% against a 9% cost of capital \u2014 a 10-point spread that is the clearest signature of an economic moat, and 25% gross margins are typical of commodity economics where competitors can replicate the product cheaply.","The business throws off $2.4B in free cash flow \u2014 roughly 7 cents on every revenue dollar, which is the owner-earnings figure that actually belongs to shareholders, and cash conversion sits at 1.27\u00d7 so those profits are backed by real cash.","On the balance sheet, leverage is comfortably conservative at 0.7\u00d7 net debt/EBITDA, and interest coverage of 12\u00d7 is fortress-like.","Shareholder yield is only 1.7%, a thin return of capital, and insider ownership is negligible, so management has little personal stake in the long-term outcome."],"sector_headwinds":[{"text":"Priced near or above estimated fair value, so the margin of safety has been bid away","sev":"amber","cat":"valuation","magnitude":0.03335027960269566},{"text":"Significant insider selling (net $6.7M)","sev":"amber","cat":"insider","dollars":-6748067.81},{"text":"News sentiment running negative (-0.18) across recent coverage","sev":"amber","cat":"news"},{"text":"Industrials sector lagging the market significantly, underperforming by 8% over 3 months","sev":"amber","cat":"sector"},{"text":"Industrials ETF trading well below its long-term trend","sev":"amber","cat":"sector"},{"text":"Cyclical sectors like Industrials tend to underperform in slowdowns","sev":"amber","cat":"sector"},{"text":"Above-average market volatility (VIX 26)","sev":"amber","cat":"macro"},{"text":"Late-cycle dynamics increase the probability of a slowdown","sev":"amber","cat":"macro"},{"text":"Cyclicality and capital intensity \u2014 order books turn on a dime, and the heavy fixed cost base that creates the moat also magnifies the downturn.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"},{"text":"Tariff and trade-policy exposure \u2014 industrial exporters sit squarely in the crosshairs of protectionist policy, and retaliatory tariffs can close markets without warning.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"}],"sector_tailwinds":["Reinvestment rate supports 20% organic growth capacity \u2014 capital is compounding inside the business","Trading near the bottom of its 52-week range \u2014 the market is offering a discount","Altman Z comfortably in the safe zone \u2014 a fortress balance sheet on this measure","41 consecutive years of dividend payments \u2014 an operating record that makes the dividend claim credible","Healthy payout ratio leaves room for both dividend growth and reinvestment"],"news_headlines":[{"title":"Trading Systems Reacting to (CMI) Volatility","source":"news.stocktradersdaily.com","link":"https://news.stocktradersdaily.com/news_release/78/Trading_Systems_Reacting_to_CMI_Volatility_110626125402_1793987642.html","date":"2026-11-06","timestamp":1793987642.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.0,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":[]},{"title":"Cummins Q3 Earnings Call Highlights","source":"thelincolnianonline.com","link":"https://www.thelincolnianonline.com/2026